<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
    WinUI's stock controls, re-templated as the Command Console's own. FluentOverrides.xaml restates the colours
    WinUI reads, which is as far as a colour can reach; this is where a control's shape changes. Three so far: the
    cap that every button takes, the bat-lever switch, and the recessed field that every text box, password box
    and number box is typed into, at the foot of the file.

    The cap. A button on the console is a machined key cut from the chassis: the palette's cap face, a key light
    across the top, the machined radius, and its word in Archivo at the cap width. The palette has written the
    three faces - plain, armed and chrome - and Fonts.xaml the cap face, since the tokens were generated; until
    this dictionary existed nothing read any of them, so the cap was a colour that could not appear.

    Three styles, and only the face differs:

      ConsoleCapButtonStyle   every button, unless it asks for another (System-X styles.css .btn, :2062)
      ArmedCapButtonStyle     a consequential command, and only those (.btn-armed, :2093)
      ChromeCapButtonStyle    a page's single polished call to action (.btn-chrome, :2116)

    The implicit style below carries nothing but ConsoleCapButtonStyle, so a button nobody styled is a cap and
    the cap is still defined in one place (ConsoleCapTests). Its variants are BasedOn it and restate a face; a
    template of their own would be the plain cap's states copied, which is what stops following it.

    Sources are the stylesheet at the revision this console is transcribed from, system-x-app@eaba14b, which
    Instruments.xaml and the token generator both name, and the line numbers are that file's. Each selector is
    written beside its line because System-X has moved on since the pin - .btn is at :1801 in its working tree
    now - and the selector is the part that survives a re-pin.

    Transcribed. The faces, the edge, the key light, the lip and the radius are the palette's and Fonts.xaml's,
    read from System-X in earlier phases. The metrics are read from it here, off the one rule that sizes .btn,
    .btn-armed, .btn-chrome and .btn-ghost together (:1984-2009): 34 high, 14 either side of the word and
    nothing above or below it, Archivo at 11.5 tracked .08em - CharacterSpacing is thousandths of an em, so 80 -
    on the 4px control radius. The word is the silver ramp's bright step, one brighter than the chip's, which the
    palette writes as SilverBrightBrush. Weight 700 and width 112% are not setters: the face is the instance
    build-fonts.py cuts at that weight and that width, so asking a Bold-only family for Bold is asking twice
    (Fonts.xaml, scripts/build-fonts.py:14). Every one of these is the same in System-X's working tree, so the
    pin costs nothing here.

    Translated, where the CSS says it in something WinUI has not got:

      hover      `filter: brightness(1.14)` and a 520ms specular glint swept across the cap. Here the key light
                 comes up and the edge sharpens. WinUI has no filter, and the glint wants a clip animated per cap.
      disabled   `opacity: .42` with `saturate(.5)`. The dimming is drawn, through the palette's per-shift
                 ConsoleDisabledOpacity, which High Contrast writes as 1 and greys the word with GrayText instead.
                 The desaturation is not: WinUI has no filter (the switch's locked state says what it would take).
      pressed    `translateY(1px)` over 80ms on the snap easing. The travel is transcribed; the 80ms is not, as a
                 visual state setter arrives at once.
      the rest   `gap: 8px` between an icon and its word, `text-transform: uppercase` and `white-space: nowrap`
                 have no Button property to carry them. Words are typed in capitals at the call site.

    Not here. System-X has since given the same rule three size variants - .btn.sm at 26 high with 10 of padding
    and 10pt, .btn.lg at 44, 22 and 13pt, and a square .btn.icon whose width is the cap's own height at each
    size. They are not in the pinned revision, so they are not transcribed, and three styles no page names would
    be three new orphans in any case: the thing this dictionary was written to end. They arrive with the page
    that asks for one, and with a re-pin, which is a decision of its own and not one to take inside a control.

    High Contrast needs nothing here. Every token below resolves to a system colour in that shift - the face to
    ButtonFace, the armed face to Highlight with HighlightText on it, the disabled word to GrayText - so the cap
    is drawn in the user's own colours without this file naming one.
-->
<ResourceDictionary
    xmlns="http://schemas.microsoft.com/winfx/2006/xaml/presentation"
    xmlns:x="http://schemas.microsoft.com/winfx/2006/xaml"
    xmlns:instruments="using:SysMonitor.App.Controls.Instruments">

    <!-- ============================================================ CAP (.btn, :2062) -->

    <Style x:Key="ConsoleCapButtonStyle" TargetType="Button">
        <Setter Property="Background" Value="{ThemeResource CapFaceBrush}"/>
        <Setter Property="Foreground" Value="{ThemeResource SilverBrightBrush}"/>
        <Setter Property="BorderBrush" Value="{ThemeResource CapEdgeBrush}"/>
        <Setter Property="BorderThickness" Value="1"/>
        <Setter Property="CornerRadius" Value="{StaticResource CapCornerRadius}"/>
        <Setter Property="Padding" Value="14,0"/>
        <Setter Property="MinHeight" Value="34"/>
        <Setter Property="HorizontalContentAlignment" Value="Center"/>
        <Setter Property="VerticalContentAlignment" Value="Center"/>
        <Setter Property="FontFamily" Value="{StaticResource ConsoleCapFontFamily}"/>
        <Setter Property="FontSize" Value="11.5"/>
        <Setter Property="CharacterSpacing" Value="80"/>
        <Setter Property="UseSystemFocusVisuals" Value="True"/>
        <Setter Property="Template">
            <Setter.Value>
                <ControlTemplate TargetType="Button">
                    <Grid x:Name="Root" MinHeight="{TemplateBinding MinHeight}"
                          Background="Transparent" CornerRadius="{TemplateBinding CornerRadius}">

                        <!-- The cap moves under the finger, so the whole key travels, face and word together. -->
                        <Grid.RenderTransform>
                            <TranslateTransform x:Name="Press"/>
                        </Grid.RenderTransform>

                        <VisualStateManager.VisualStateGroups>
                            <VisualStateGroup x:Name="CommonStates">
                                <VisualState x:Name="Normal"/>

                                <!-- Under the pointer the key light comes up and the edge sharpens. -->
                                <VisualState x:Name="PointerOver">
                                    <VisualState.Setters>
                                        <Setter Target="KeyLight.Opacity" Value="1"/>
                                        <Setter Target="Face.BorderBrush" Value="{ThemeResource HairlineStrongBrush}"/>
                                    </VisualState.Setters>
                                </VisualState>

                                <!-- Pressed, it goes in: the key light off, the lip gone, the key down one pixel. -->
                                <VisualState x:Name="Pressed">
                                    <VisualState.Setters>
                                        <Setter Target="KeyLight.Opacity" Value="0"/>
                                        <Setter Target="Lip.Opacity" Value="0"/>
                                        <Setter Target="Press.Y" Value="1"/>
                                    </VisualState.Setters>
                                </VisualState>

                                <!-- Locked: opacity .42 (:2016-2023). The key light and the lip go with it - a
                                     cap nobody can press is not catching the light - and the word takes the
                                     shift's own locked colour, which is the user's GrayText in High Contrast.
                                     That shift leaves ConsoleDisabledOpacity at 1: dimming a control against a
                                     ground the user chose for its contrast is the one thing it must not do. -->
                                <VisualState x:Name="Disabled">
                                    <VisualState.Setters>
                                        <Setter Target="Root.Opacity" Value="{ThemeResource ConsoleDisabledOpacity}"/>
                                        <Setter Target="KeyLight.Opacity" Value="0"/>
                                        <Setter Target="Lip.Opacity" Value="0"/>
                                        <Setter Target="Word.Foreground" Value="{ThemeResource ConsoleDisabledForegroundBrush}"/>
                                    </VisualState.Setters>
                                </VisualState>
                            </VisualStateGroup>
                        </VisualStateManager.VisualStateGroups>

                        <Border x:Name="Face" Background="{TemplateBinding Background}"
                                BorderBrush="{TemplateBinding BorderBrush}"
                                BorderThickness="{TemplateBinding BorderThickness}"
                                CornerRadius="{TemplateBinding CornerRadius}"/>

                        <Border x:Name="KeyLight" Opacity="0.85" Margin="1"
                                Background="{ThemeResource CapKeyLightBrush}"
                                CornerRadius="{TemplateBinding CornerRadius}"
                                IsHitTestVisible="False"/>

                        <Border x:Name="Lip" Height="1" Margin="1,1,1,0" VerticalAlignment="Top"
                                Background="{ThemeResource PlateLipBrush}" IsHitTestVisible="False"/>

                        <ContentPresenter x:Name="Word" Content="{TemplateBinding Content}"
                                          ContentTemplate="{TemplateBinding ContentTemplate}"
                                          ContentTransitions="{TemplateBinding ContentTransitions}"
                                          Padding="{TemplateBinding Padding}"
                                          HorizontalAlignment="{TemplateBinding HorizontalContentAlignment}"
                                          VerticalAlignment="{TemplateBinding VerticalContentAlignment}"
                                          FontFamily="{TemplateBinding FontFamily}"
                                          FontSize="{TemplateBinding FontSize}"
                                          CharacterSpacing="{TemplateBinding CharacterSpacing}"
                                          Foreground="{TemplateBinding Foreground}"
                                          AutomationProperties.AccessibilityView="Raw"/>
                    </Grid>
                </ControlTemplate>
            </Setter.Value>
        </Setter>
    </Style>

    <!-- A button that asks for nothing is a cap. This is the only reason that is true: a keyed style is never
         applied by itself. It adds nothing, so the cap stays defined once, above. -->
    <Style TargetType="Button" BasedOn="{StaticResource ConsoleCapButtonStyle}"/>

    <!-- Armed (.btn-armed, :2093): consequential commands only - wiping, deleting, anything that cannot simply be undone.
         ArmedFg is the warm white System-X writes on armed red, and the one FluentOverrides already puts on
         WinUI's accent, so an armed cap and an accent control read the same. -->
    <Style x:Key="ArmedCapButtonStyle" TargetType="Button" BasedOn="{StaticResource ConsoleCapButtonStyle}">
        <Setter Property="Background" Value="{ThemeResource ArmedCapFaceBrush}"/>
        <Setter Property="Foreground" Value="{ThemeResource ArmedFgBrush}"/>
        <Setter Property="BorderBrush" Value="{ThemeResource ArmedEdgeBrush}"/>
    </Style>

    <!-- Chrome (.btn-chrome, :2116): the one polished call to action on a page, black gloss on Day Shift. -->
    <Style x:Key="ChromeCapButtonStyle" TargetType="Button" BasedOn="{StaticResource ConsoleCapButtonStyle}">
        <Setter Property="Background" Value="{ThemeResource ChromeCapFaceBrush}"/>
        <Setter Property="Foreground" Value="{ThemeResource ChromeCapForegroundBrush}"/>
        <Setter Property="BorderBrush" Value="{ThemeResource ChromeEdgeBrush}"/>
    </Style>
    <!-- ============================================================ BAT-LEVER SWITCH (.switch, :2323) -->

    <!-- A switch on the console is a lever, not a pill: a recess cut into the chassis with a machined cap for a
         thumb, armed red when it is on. FluentOverrides.xaml can only reach the colours, so the shape is cut here.

         WinUI's own parts are kept, name for name, because ToggleSwitch's code drives them. It measures
         SwitchKnobBounds against SwitchKnob to know how far the knob travels and how far a drag may go, writes
         KnobTranslateTransform while a finger drags it, and puts the focus rectangle on SwitchAreaGrid. A template
         that renames one of them still builds and still draws, and loses what that part drove with nothing to say
         so, which is why the list of them is a test (ConsoleSwitchTests). The header and the on and off words stay
         for the same reason: the pages use both.

         The travel is the transcribed 160ms on the snap easing (:2347), animating KnobTranslateTransform rather
         than WinUI's reposition animation, which moved the knob element instead. A drag writes that same transform,
         so every state that rests the thumb says where it rests (Off, below), and the smoke run reproduces what a
         drag leaves behind (UiSmokeRun.CheckSwitchDragAsync). -->
    <Style TargetType="ToggleSwitch">
        <Setter Property="instruments:ConsoleLever.HasGlows" Value="True"/>
        <Setter Property="Foreground" Value="{ThemeResource SilverBrush}"/>
        <Setter Property="FontFamily" Value="{StaticResource ConsoleBodyFontFamily}"/>
        <Setter Property="FontSize" Value="13"/>
        <Setter Property="HorizontalAlignment" Value="Left"/>
        <Setter Property="VerticalAlignment" Value="Center"/>
        <Setter Property="HorizontalContentAlignment" Value="Left"/>
        <Setter Property="VerticalContentAlignment" Value="Center"/>
        <Setter Property="ManipulationMode" Value="System,TranslateX"/>
        <Setter Property="UseSystemFocusVisuals" Value="True"/>
        <Setter Property="FocusVisualMargin" Value="-3"/>
        <Setter Property="Template">
            <Setter.Value>
                <ControlTemplate TargetType="ToggleSwitch">
                    <Grid x:Name="Root">
                        <Grid.RowDefinitions>
                            <RowDefinition Height="Auto"/>
                            <RowDefinition Height="*"/>
                        </Grid.RowDefinitions>

                        <VisualStateManager.VisualStateGroups>
                            <VisualStateGroup x:Name="CommonStates">
                                <VisualState x:Name="Normal"/>

                                <!-- Under the pointer the recess edge sharpens, as a cap's does. -->
                                <VisualState x:Name="PointerOver">
                                    <VisualState.Setters>
                                        <Setter Target="OuterBorder.BorderBrush" Value="{ThemeResource HairlineStrongBrush}"/>
                                    </VisualState.Setters>
                                </VisualState>

                                <VisualState x:Name="Pressed"/>

                                <!-- Locked: opacity .42 (:2365-2369), which is the caps' treatment, which is
                                     what the stylesheet asks for in as many words - the same rule is written
                                     for the buttons at :2016 and pointed at from here "so a locked control
                                     reads the same way everywhere on the console rather than inventing a second
                                     idiom". It dims through one resource the palette writes per shift, and High
                                     Contrast writes 1 for it: dimming a control against a ground the user chose
                                     for its contrast is the one thing that shift must not do, so it greys the
                                     words with the user's own GrayText instead.

                                     `filter: saturate(.5)` is not drawn. WinUI has no filter, and the only
                                     route to it is a desaturated twin of every armed face the lever can show,
                                     generated beside the original. Dimming carries the meaning on its own;
                                     desaturating a red that is already dimmed to .42 is the smaller half. -->
                                <VisualState x:Name="Disabled">
                                    <VisualState.Setters>
                                        <Setter Target="Root.Opacity" Value="{ThemeResource ConsoleDisabledOpacity}"/>
                                        <Setter Target="HeaderContentPresenter.Foreground" Value="{ThemeResource ConsoleDisabledForegroundBrush}"/>
                                        <Setter Target="OnContentPresenter.Foreground" Value="{ThemeResource ConsoleDisabledForegroundBrush}"/>
                                        <Setter Target="OffContentPresenter.Foreground" Value="{ThemeResource ConsoleDisabledForegroundBrush}"/>
                                    </VisualState.Setters>
                                </VisualState>
                            </VisualStateGroup>

                            <VisualStateGroup x:Name="ToggleStates">
                                <VisualStateGroup.Transitions>
                                    <VisualTransition x:Name="DraggingToOnTransition" From="Dragging" To="On" GeneratedDuration="0">
                                        <Storyboard>
                                            <DoubleAnimationUsingKeyFrames Storyboard.TargetName="KnobTranslateTransform" Storyboard.TargetProperty="X">
                                                <SplineDoubleKeyFrame KeyTime="0:0:0.16" Value="20" KeySpline="0.32,0.72 0,1"/>
                                            </DoubleAnimationUsingKeyFrames>
                                            <DoubleAnimationUsingKeyFrames Storyboard.TargetName="SwitchKnobBounds" Storyboard.TargetProperty="Opacity">
                                                <LinearDoubleKeyFrame KeyTime="0:0:0.16" Value="1"/>
                                            </DoubleAnimationUsingKeyFrames>
                                            <DoubleAnimationUsingKeyFrames Storyboard.TargetName="ArmedRim" Storyboard.TargetProperty="Opacity">
                                                <LinearDoubleKeyFrame KeyTime="0:0:0.16" Value="1"/>
                                            </DoubleAnimationUsingKeyFrames>
                                            <DoubleAnimationUsingKeyFrames Storyboard.TargetName="SwitchKnobOn" Storyboard.TargetProperty="Opacity">
                                                <LinearDoubleKeyFrame KeyTime="0:0:0.16" Value="1"/>
                                            </DoubleAnimationUsingKeyFrames>
                                            <DoubleAnimationUsingKeyFrames Storyboard.TargetName="SwitchKnobOff" Storyboard.TargetProperty="Opacity">
                                                <LinearDoubleKeyFrame KeyTime="0:0:0.16" Value="0"/>
                                            </DoubleAnimationUsingKeyFrames>
                                        </Storyboard>
                                    </VisualTransition>

                                    <VisualTransition x:Name="OnToDraggingTransition" From="On" To="Dragging" GeneratedDuration="0">
                                        <Storyboard>
                                            <DoubleAnimationUsingKeyFrames Storyboard.TargetName="SwitchKnobBounds" Storyboard.TargetProperty="Opacity">
                                                <LinearDoubleKeyFrame KeyTime="0" Value="1"/>
                                            </DoubleAnimationUsingKeyFrames>
                                            <DoubleAnimationUsingKeyFrames Storyboard.TargetName="ArmedRim" Storyboard.TargetProperty="Opacity">
                                                <LinearDoubleKeyFrame KeyTime="0" Value="1"/>
                                            </DoubleAnimationUsingKeyFrames>
                                            <DoubleAnimationUsingKeyFrames Storyboard.TargetName="SwitchKnobOn" Storyboard.TargetProperty="Opacity">
                                                <LinearDoubleKeyFrame KeyTime="0" Value="1"/>
                                            </DoubleAnimationUsingKeyFrames>
                                            <DoubleAnimationUsingKeyFrames Storyboard.TargetName="SwitchKnobOff" Storyboard.TargetProperty="Opacity">
                                                <LinearDoubleKeyFrame KeyTime="0" Value="0"/>
                                            </DoubleAnimationUsingKeyFrames>
                                        </Storyboard>
                                    </VisualTransition>

                                    <VisualTransition x:Name="DraggingToOffTransition" From="Dragging" To="Off" GeneratedDuration="0">
                                        <Storyboard>
                                            <DoubleAnimationUsingKeyFrames Storyboard.TargetName="KnobTranslateTransform" Storyboard.TargetProperty="X">
                                                <SplineDoubleKeyFrame KeyTime="0:0:0.16" Value="0" KeySpline="0.32,0.72 0,1"/>
                                            </DoubleAnimationUsingKeyFrames>
                                            <DoubleAnimationUsingKeyFrames Storyboard.TargetName="SwitchKnobBounds" Storyboard.TargetProperty="Opacity">
                                                <LinearDoubleKeyFrame KeyTime="0:0:0.16" Value="0"/>
                                            </DoubleAnimationUsingKeyFrames>
                                            <DoubleAnimationUsingKeyFrames Storyboard.TargetName="ArmedRim" Storyboard.TargetProperty="Opacity">
                                                <LinearDoubleKeyFrame KeyTime="0:0:0.16" Value="0"/>
                                            </DoubleAnimationUsingKeyFrames>
                                            <DoubleAnimationUsingKeyFrames Storyboard.TargetName="SwitchKnobOn" Storyboard.TargetProperty="Opacity">
                                                <LinearDoubleKeyFrame KeyTime="0:0:0.16" Value="0"/>
                                            </DoubleAnimationUsingKeyFrames>
                                            <DoubleAnimationUsingKeyFrames Storyboard.TargetName="SwitchKnobOff" Storyboard.TargetProperty="Opacity">
                                                <LinearDoubleKeyFrame KeyTime="0:0:0.16" Value="1"/>
                                            </DoubleAnimationUsingKeyFrames>
                                        </Storyboard>
                                    </VisualTransition>

                                    <VisualTransition x:Name="OnToOffTransition" From="On" To="Off" GeneratedDuration="0">
                                        <Storyboard>
                                            <DoubleAnimationUsingKeyFrames Storyboard.TargetName="KnobTranslateTransform" Storyboard.TargetProperty="X">
                                                <SplineDoubleKeyFrame KeyTime="0:0:0.16" Value="0" KeySpline="0.32,0.72 0,1"/>
                                            </DoubleAnimationUsingKeyFrames>
                                        </Storyboard>
                                    </VisualTransition>

                                    <VisualTransition x:Name="OffToOnTransition" From="Off" To="On" GeneratedDuration="0">
                                        <Storyboard>
                                            <DoubleAnimationUsingKeyFrames Storyboard.TargetName="KnobTranslateTransform" Storyboard.TargetProperty="X">
                                                <SplineDoubleKeyFrame KeyTime="0:0:0.16" Value="20" KeySpline="0.32,0.72 0,1"/>
                                            </DoubleAnimationUsingKeyFrames>
                                            <DoubleAnimationUsingKeyFrames Storyboard.TargetName="SwitchKnobBounds" Storyboard.TargetProperty="Opacity">
                                                <LinearDoubleKeyFrame KeyTime="0:0:0.16" Value="1"/>
                                            </DoubleAnimationUsingKeyFrames>
                                            <DoubleAnimationUsingKeyFrames Storyboard.TargetName="ArmedRim" Storyboard.TargetProperty="Opacity">
                                                <LinearDoubleKeyFrame KeyTime="0:0:0.16" Value="1"/>
                                            </DoubleAnimationUsingKeyFrames>
                                            <DoubleAnimationUsingKeyFrames Storyboard.TargetName="SwitchKnobOn" Storyboard.TargetProperty="Opacity">
                                                <LinearDoubleKeyFrame KeyTime="0:0:0.16" Value="1"/>
                                            </DoubleAnimationUsingKeyFrames>
                                            <DoubleAnimationUsingKeyFrames Storyboard.TargetName="SwitchKnobOff" Storyboard.TargetProperty="Opacity">
                                                <LinearDoubleKeyFrame KeyTime="0:0:0.16" Value="0"/>
                                            </DoubleAnimationUsingKeyFrames>
                                        </Storyboard>
                                    </VisualTransition>
                                </VisualStateGroup.Transitions>

                                <VisualState x:Name="Dragging"/>

                                <!-- Off puts the thumb back at the left, and has to say so rather than leave it
                                     to the transform's own value: a drag writes that value, so a lever that was
                                     dragged and then turned off would leave its thumb wherever the finger let
                                     go of it. The travel there is the transition's; this is where it rests. -->
                                <VisualState x:Name="Off">
                                    <Storyboard>
                                        <DoubleAnimation Storyboard.TargetName="KnobTranslateTransform" Storyboard.TargetProperty="X" To="0" Duration="0"/>
                                    </Storyboard>
                                </VisualState>

                                <!-- On: the thumb sits 20 over, which is translateX(20px) and also exactly
                                     SwitchKnobBounds less SwitchKnob, the distance WinUI works out for a drag. -->
                                <VisualState x:Name="On">
                                    <Storyboard>
                                        <DoubleAnimation Storyboard.TargetName="KnobTranslateTransform" Storyboard.TargetProperty="X" To="20" Duration="0"/>
                                        <DoubleAnimationUsingKeyFrames Storyboard.TargetName="SwitchKnobBounds" Storyboard.TargetProperty="Opacity">
                                            <LinearDoubleKeyFrame KeyTime="0:0:0.16" Value="1"/>
                                        </DoubleAnimationUsingKeyFrames>
                                        <DoubleAnimationUsingKeyFrames Storyboard.TargetName="ArmedRim" Storyboard.TargetProperty="Opacity">
                                            <LinearDoubleKeyFrame KeyTime="0:0:0.16" Value="1"/>
                                        </DoubleAnimationUsingKeyFrames>
                                        <DoubleAnimationUsingKeyFrames Storyboard.TargetName="SwitchKnobOn" Storyboard.TargetProperty="Opacity">
                                            <LinearDoubleKeyFrame KeyTime="0:0:0.16" Value="1"/>
                                        </DoubleAnimationUsingKeyFrames>
                                        <DoubleAnimationUsingKeyFrames Storyboard.TargetName="SwitchKnobOff" Storyboard.TargetProperty="Opacity">
                                            <LinearDoubleKeyFrame KeyTime="0:0:0.16" Value="0"/>
                                        </DoubleAnimationUsingKeyFrames>
                                    </Storyboard>
                                </VisualState>
                            </VisualStateGroup>

                            <VisualStateGroup x:Name="ContentStates">
                                <VisualState x:Name="OffContent">
                                    <Storyboard>
                                        <DoubleAnimation Storyboard.TargetName="OffContentPresenter" Storyboard.TargetProperty="Opacity" To="1" Duration="0"/>
                                        <ObjectAnimationUsingKeyFrames Storyboard.TargetName="OffContentPresenter" Storyboard.TargetProperty="IsHitTestVisible">
                                            <DiscreteObjectKeyFrame KeyTime="0" Value="True"/>
                                        </ObjectAnimationUsingKeyFrames>
                                    </Storyboard>
                                </VisualState>
                                <VisualState x:Name="OnContent">
                                    <Storyboard>
                                        <DoubleAnimation Storyboard.TargetName="OnContentPresenter" Storyboard.TargetProperty="Opacity" To="1" Duration="0"/>
                                        <ObjectAnimationUsingKeyFrames Storyboard.TargetName="OnContentPresenter" Storyboard.TargetProperty="IsHitTestVisible">
                                            <DiscreteObjectKeyFrame KeyTime="0" Value="True"/>
                                        </ObjectAnimationUsingKeyFrames>
                                    </Storyboard>
                                </VisualState>
                            </VisualStateGroup>
                        </VisualStateManager.VisualStateGroups>

                        <ContentPresenter x:Name="HeaderContentPresenter"
                                          Grid.Row="0"
                                          Content="{TemplateBinding Header}"
                                          ContentTemplate="{TemplateBinding HeaderTemplate}"
                                          Foreground="{TemplateBinding Foreground}"
                                          FontFamily="{TemplateBinding FontFamily}"
                                          FontSize="{TemplateBinding FontSize}"
                                          Margin="0,0,0,6"
                                          TextWrapping="Wrap"
                                          VerticalAlignment="Top"
                                          Visibility="Collapsed"
                                          AutomationProperties.AccessibilityView="Raw"/>

                        <Grid Grid.Row="1" HorizontalAlignment="Left" VerticalAlignment="Center">
                            <Grid.ColumnDefinitions>
                                <ColumnDefinition Width="Auto"/>
                                <ColumnDefinition Width="12" MaxWidth="12"/>
                                <ColumnDefinition Width="Auto"/>
                            </Grid.ColumnDefinitions>

                            <Grid x:Name="SwitchAreaGrid" Grid.ColumnSpan="3" Background="Transparent"
                                  CornerRadius="{StaticResource CapCornerRadius}"
                                  Control.IsTemplateFocusTarget="True"/>

                            <ContentPresenter x:Name="OffContentPresenter" Grid.Column="2" Opacity="0"
                                              Content="{TemplateBinding OffContent}"
                                              ContentTemplate="{TemplateBinding OffContentTemplate}"
                                              Foreground="{TemplateBinding Foreground}"
                                              FontFamily="{TemplateBinding FontFamily}"
                                              FontSize="{TemplateBinding FontSize}"
                                              IsHitTestVisible="False"
                                              HorizontalAlignment="{TemplateBinding HorizontalContentAlignment}"
                                              VerticalAlignment="Center"
                                              AutomationProperties.AccessibilityView="Raw"/>

                            <ContentPresenter x:Name="OnContentPresenter" Grid.Column="2" Opacity="0"
                                              Content="{TemplateBinding OnContent}"
                                              ContentTemplate="{TemplateBinding OnContentTemplate}"
                                              Foreground="{TemplateBinding Foreground}"
                                              FontFamily="{TemplateBinding FontFamily}"
                                              FontSize="{TemplateBinding FontSize}"
                                              IsHitTestVisible="False"
                                              HorizontalAlignment="{TemplateBinding HorizontalContentAlignment}"
                                              VerticalAlignment="Center"
                                              AutomationProperties.AccessibilityView="Raw"/>

                            <!-- The palette's armed glow, carried into the template so ConsoleLever can read
                                 it without knowing which shift it is in. Drawn by nothing; it is a colour. -->
                            <Border x:Name="PART_ArmedGlow" Visibility="Collapsed"
                                    Background="{ThemeResource ArmedGlowBrush}"/>

                            <!-- Armed, the track glows 0 0 12px outside itself (:2352). Composition casts it
                                 from ConsoleLever onto this host, which sits under the track. -->
                            <Border x:Name="PART_TrackGlowHost" Width="42" Height="22" IsHitTestVisible="False"/>

                            <!-- The recess: the track, its edge, and the shade the top edge casts into it. -->
                            <Border x:Name="OuterBorder" Width="42" Height="22"
                                    Background="{ThemeResource SwitchTrackBrush}"
                                    BorderBrush="{ThemeResource SwitchEdgeBrush}"
                                    BorderThickness="1"
                                    CornerRadius="{StaticResource CapCornerRadius}"/>

                            <!-- Armed, the rim goes to armed deep and the track to the armed recess. -->
                            <Border x:Name="ArmedRim" Width="42" Height="22" Opacity="0"
                                    BorderBrush="{ThemeResource ArmedDeepBrush}"
                                    BorderThickness="1"
                                    CornerRadius="{StaticResource CapCornerRadius}"
                                    IsHitTestVisible="False"/>

                            <!-- Inside the 1px edge: 40 by 20, which is what the knob travels in. -->
                            <Grid Width="40" Height="20">
                                <Border x:Name="SwitchKnobBounds" Width="40" Height="20" Opacity="0"
                                        Background="{ThemeResource SwitchTrackArmedBrush}"
                                        CornerRadius="{StaticResource InsetCornerRadius}"
                                        IsHitTestVisible="False"/>

                                <Border x:Name="Shade" Height="4" VerticalAlignment="Top"
                                        Background="{ThemeResource SwitchShadeTopBrush}"
                                        IsHitTestVisible="False"/>

                                <Grid x:Name="SwitchKnob" Width="20" Height="20" HorizontalAlignment="Left">
                                    <!-- The thumb's own glow, 0 0 10px (:2359). Inside SwitchKnob, so it
                                         travels with the thumb instead of staying at the left of the track. -->
                                    <Border x:Name="PART_ThumbGlowHost" Width="16" Height="16"
                                            IsHitTestVisible="False"/>

                                    <Border x:Name="SwitchKnobOff" Width="16" Height="16"
                                            Background="{ThemeResource SwitchThumbBrush}"
                                            CornerRadius="{StaticResource InsetCornerRadius}">
                                        <Border Height="1" VerticalAlignment="Top" Margin="1,0"
                                                Background="{ThemeResource SwitchThumbLipBrush}"/>
                                    </Border>

                                    <Border x:Name="SwitchKnobOn" Width="16" Height="16" Opacity="0"
                                            Background="{ThemeResource SwitchThumbArmedBrush}"
                                            CornerRadius="{StaticResource InsetCornerRadius}">
                                        <Border Height="1" VerticalAlignment="Top" Margin="1,0"
                                                Background="{ThemeResource SwitchThumbArmedLipBrush}"/>
                                    </Border>

                                    <Grid.RenderTransform>
                                        <TranslateTransform x:Name="KnobTranslateTransform"/>
                                    </Grid.RenderTransform>
                                </Grid>
                            </Grid>

                            <Thumb x:Name="SwitchThumb" Grid.ColumnSpan="3"
                                   AutomationProperties.AccessibilityView="Raw">
                                <Thumb.Template>
                                    <ControlTemplate TargetType="Thumb">
                                        <Rectangle Fill="Transparent"/>
                                    </ControlTemplate>
                                </Thumb.Template>
                            </Thumb>
                        </Grid>
                    </Grid>
                </ControlTemplate>
            </Setter.Value>
        </Setter>
    </Style>

    <!-- ============================================================ FIELD (.field, :2286) -->

    <!-- A form field on the console is a recessed dark well cut into the plate, dark in both shifts - the
         stylesheet says so in as many words above the rule (:2285) - so its face, edge and words are the same on
         Day Shift as on Night Ops. Three controls are typed into and take it: TextBox, PasswordBox, and NumberBox,
         whose own text box is pointed at the same style. ComboBox is not one: System-X gives `select` no .field
         rule, only the armed accent (:999-1003), and FluentOverrides already carries that.

         WinUI's own templates are kept part for part, because each control's code finds its parts by name -
         ContentElement is where the text is drawn, PlaceholderTextContentPresenter where the hint is, DeleteButton
         and RevealButton are found and shown by the control, and NumberBox drives InputBox, its spin buttons and
         their popup. A template that renames one still builds and still draws, and loses what the part did, which
         is why the list of them is a test (ConsoleFieldTests). The colour states are the console's.

         Transcribed: 8 above and below the words and 11 either side, the 4px control radius, Public Sans 13, the
         face's gradient and its 1px edge, the shade the top edge casts in (inset 0 2px 4px, drawn as a gradient
         because WinUI has no inset shadow, as the switch's recess is) and the light along the lower lip (inset 0
         -1px 0). The placeholder is its own grey (:2300). Focused, the edge goes to armed edge and a 2px armed
         outline stands 1px off it (:2303): drawn here, not left to the system focus rectangle, because that only
         shows for the keyboard and a browser shows a text field's on any focus. A header is a field label (:2312):
         Departure Mono 10, tracked .12em, 5 above its field, in silver mute - FieldLabelTextStyle's values, which a
         presenter cannot take as a TextBlock style. Words are typed in capitals at the call site, as everywhere.

         The well's own parts - its text, its clear and reveal buttons, NumberBox's inline spinners - ask for the
         dark theme, as a Well or a Display does. Their text and glyph colours, and the caret, follow the element's
         theme rather than its Foreground, so on Day Shift they would otherwise come out dark on a dark well.

         Translated or not drawn:

           transition  `border-color 160ms` on the out easing. A visual state setter arrives at once.
           hover       none: the stylesheet gives a field no hover rule, so PointerOver changes nothing.
           .invalid    the warn edge (:2308) has no WinUI state to hang on and no page that validates a field. It
                       arrives with the first page that does.
           locked      the console's one locked idiom (:2016-2023): the field dims by ConsoleDisabledOpacity, its
                       label takes the shared locked word, and its own words take the field's twin of it - the
                       chassis' locked word is dark on Day Shift and would vanish into the well. Both are GrayText
                       in High Contrast, which does not dim.

         High Contrast needs nothing here: the face is Window, the edge and the words WindowText, the placeholder
         GrayText, armed edge and display Highlight, and the shade and lip go. -->
    <Style x:Key="ConsoleFieldTextBoxStyle" TargetType="TextBox" BasedOn="{StaticResource DefaultTextBoxStyle}">
        <Setter Property="Foreground" Value="{ThemeResource FieldForegroundBrush}"/>
        <Setter Property="Background" Value="{ThemeResource FieldFaceBrush}"/>
        <Setter Property="BorderBrush" Value="{ThemeResource FieldEdgeBrush}"/>
        <Setter Property="PlaceholderForeground" Value="{ThemeResource FieldPlaceholderBrush}"/>
        <Setter Property="BorderThickness" Value="1"/>
        <Setter Property="CornerRadius" Value="{StaticResource CapCornerRadius}"/>
        <Setter Property="Padding" Value="11,8"/>
        <Setter Property="FontFamily" Value="{StaticResource ConsoleBodyFontFamily}"/>
        <Setter Property="FontSize" Value="13"/>
        <Setter Property="UseSystemFocusVisuals" Value="False"/>
        <Setter Property="Template">
            <Setter.Value>
                <ControlTemplate TargetType="TextBox">
                    <Grid x:Name="Root">

                        <Grid.Resources>
                            <!-- WinUI's clear button, as it draws it. -->
                            <Style x:Key="FieldClearButtonStyle" TargetType="Button">
                                <Setter Property="Template">
                                    <Setter.Value>
                                        <ControlTemplate TargetType="Button">
                                            <Grid x:Name="ButtonLayoutGrid" Margin="{ThemeResource TextBoxInnerButtonMargin}"
                                                  BorderBrush="{ThemeResource TextControlButtonBorderBrush}"
                                                  BorderThickness="{TemplateBinding BorderThickness}"
                                                  Background="{ThemeResource TextControlButtonBackground}"
                                                  BackgroundSizing="{TemplateBinding BackgroundSizing}"
                                                  CornerRadius="{TemplateBinding CornerRadius}">
                                                <VisualStateManager.VisualStateGroups>
                                                    <VisualStateGroup x:Name="CommonStates">
                                                        <VisualState x:Name="Normal"/>
                                                        <VisualState x:Name="PointerOver">
                                                            <VisualState.Setters>
                                                                <Setter Target="ButtonLayoutGrid.Background" Value="{ThemeResource TextControlButtonBackgroundPointerOver}"/>
                                                                <Setter Target="ButtonLayoutGrid.BorderBrush" Value="{ThemeResource TextControlButtonBorderBrushPointerOver}"/>
                                                                <Setter Target="GlyphElement.Foreground" Value="{ThemeResource TextControlButtonForegroundPointerOver}"/>
                                                            </VisualState.Setters>
                                                        </VisualState>
                                                        <VisualState x:Name="Pressed">
                                                            <VisualState.Setters>
                                                                <Setter Target="ButtonLayoutGrid.Background" Value="{ThemeResource TextControlButtonBackgroundPressed}"/>
                                                                <Setter Target="ButtonLayoutGrid.BorderBrush" Value="{ThemeResource TextControlButtonBorderBrushPressed}"/>
                                                                <Setter Target="GlyphElement.Foreground" Value="{ThemeResource TextControlButtonForegroundPressed}"/>
                                                            </VisualState.Setters>
                                                        </VisualState>
                                                        <!-- No Disabled state: WinUI's hid the clear button on a locked field, but the field only
                                                             shows it while it is focused, and a locked field cannot be. So it is never seen locked,
                                                             and the field's own locked state dims everything in it. -->
                                                    </VisualStateGroup>
                                                </VisualStateManager.VisualStateGroups>
                                                <TextBlock x:Name="GlyphElement" Foreground="{ThemeResource TextControlButtonForeground}"
                                                           VerticalAlignment="Center" HorizontalAlignment="Center" FontStyle="Normal"
                                                           FontSize="{ThemeResource TextBoxIconFontSize}" Text="&#xE894;"
                                                           FontFamily="{ThemeResource SymbolThemeFontFamily}"
                                                           AutomationProperties.AccessibilityView="Raw"/>
                                            </Grid>
                                        </ControlTemplate>
                                    </Setter.Value>
                                </Setter>
                            </Style>
                        </Grid.Resources>

                        <VisualStateManager.VisualStateGroups>
                            <VisualStateGroup x:Name="CommonStates">
                                <VisualState x:Name="Normal"/>

                                <!-- No hover rule in the stylesheet, so nothing changes under the pointer. -->
                                <VisualState x:Name="PointerOver"/>

                                <!-- Focused: armed edge, and the 2px armed outline 1px off it (:2303). -->
                                <VisualState x:Name="Focused">
                                    <VisualState.Setters>
                                        <Setter Target="BorderElement.BorderBrush" Value="{ThemeResource ArmedEdgeBrush}"/>
                                        <Setter Target="FocusOutline.Opacity" Value="1"/>
                                    </VisualState.Setters>
                                </VisualState>

                                <!-- Locked: the console's one idiom (:2016-2023), described above. -->
                                <VisualState x:Name="Disabled">
                                    <VisualState.Setters>
                                        <Setter Target="Root.Opacity" Value="{ThemeResource ConsoleDisabledOpacity}"/>
                                        <Setter Target="HeaderContentPresenter.Foreground" Value="{ThemeResource ConsoleDisabledForegroundBrush}"/>
                                        <Setter Target="ContentElement.Foreground" Value="{ThemeResource ConsoleDisabledFieldForegroundBrush}"/>
                                    </VisualState.Setters>
                                </VisualState>
                            </VisualStateGroup>

                            <VisualStateGroup x:Name="ButtonStates">
                                <VisualState x:Name="ButtonVisible">
                                    <VisualState.Setters>
                                        <Setter Target="DeleteButton.Visibility" Value="Visible"/>
                                    </VisualState.Setters>
                                </VisualState>
                                <VisualState x:Name="ButtonCollapsed"/>
                            </VisualStateGroup>

                            <!-- Only NumberBox's own text box is ever sent to these, by NumberBox: room for its
                                 inline spinners, or the compact popup's indicator. A plain field never leaves
                                 SpinButtonsCollapsed, where the column is empty and takes no width. -->
                            <VisualStateGroup x:Name="SpinButtonStates">
                                <VisualState x:Name="SpinButtonsCollapsed"/>
                                <VisualState x:Name="SpinButtonsPopup">
                                    <VisualState.Setters>
                                        <Setter Target="PopupIndicator.Visibility" Value="Visible"/>
                                    </VisualState.Setters>
                                </VisualState>
                                <VisualState x:Name="SpinButtonsVisible">
                                    <VisualState.Setters>
                                        <Setter Target="SpinButtonsColumn.Width" Value="72"/>
                                    </VisualState.Setters>
                                </VisualState>
                            </VisualStateGroup>
                        </VisualStateManager.VisualStateGroups>

                        <Grid.RowDefinitions>
                            <RowDefinition Height="Auto"/>
                            <RowDefinition Height="*"/>
                            <RowDefinition Height="Auto"/>
                        </Grid.RowDefinitions>

                        <Grid.ColumnDefinitions>
                            <ColumnDefinition Width="*"/>
                            <ColumnDefinition Width="Auto"/>
                            <ColumnDefinition x:Name="SpinButtonsColumn" Width="Auto"/>
                        </Grid.ColumnDefinitions>

                        <!-- The field label (:2312). -->
                        <ContentPresenter x:Name="HeaderContentPresenter" Grid.Row="0" Grid.Column="0" Grid.ColumnSpan="3"
                                          Content="{TemplateBinding Header}" ContentTemplate="{TemplateBinding HeaderTemplate}"
                                          FontFamily="{StaticResource ConsoleTelemetryFontFamily}" FontSize="10"
                                          CharacterSpacing="120" FontWeight="Normal"
                                          Foreground="{ThemeResource SilverMuteBrush}" Margin="0,0,0,5"
                                          TextWrapping="Wrap" VerticalAlignment="Top"
                                          Visibility="Collapsed" x:DeferLoadStrategy="Lazy"/>

                        <!-- outline: 2px solid armed display, offset 1px - so it stands 3 outside the edge, and
                             its corners follow the 4px radius out to 7. Shown only while focused. -->
                        <Border x:Name="FocusOutline" Grid.Row="1" Grid.Column="0" Grid.ColumnSpan="3" Margin="-3"
                                BorderBrush="{ThemeResource ArmedDisplayBrush}" BorderThickness="2" CornerRadius="7"
                                Opacity="0" IsHitTestVisible="False"/>

                        <Border x:Name="BorderElement" Grid.Row="1" Grid.Column="0" Grid.RowSpan="1" Grid.ColumnSpan="3"
                                Background="{TemplateBinding Background}" BorderBrush="{TemplateBinding BorderBrush}"
                                BorderThickness="{TemplateBinding BorderThickness}" CornerRadius="{TemplateBinding CornerRadius}"
                                Control.IsTemplateFocusTarget="True"
                                MinWidth="{TemplateBinding MinWidth}" MinHeight="{TemplateBinding MinHeight}"/>

                        <!-- The recess: the shade the top edge casts in, and the light along the lower lip, both
                             inside the 1px edge. -->
                        <Border x:Name="Shade" Grid.Row="1" Grid.Column="0" Grid.ColumnSpan="3" Height="4" Margin="1,1,1,0"
                                VerticalAlignment="Top" CornerRadius="3,3,0,0"
                                Background="{ThemeResource FieldShadeTopBrush}" IsHitTestVisible="False"/>
                        <Border x:Name="Lip" Grid.Row="1" Grid.Column="0" Grid.ColumnSpan="3" Height="1" Margin="1,0,1,1"
                                VerticalAlignment="Bottom"
                                Background="{ThemeResource FieldLipBrush}" IsHitTestVisible="False"/>

                        <ScrollViewer x:Name="ContentElement" Grid.Row="1" Grid.Column="0" RequestedTheme="Dark"
                                      HorizontalScrollMode="{TemplateBinding ScrollViewer.HorizontalScrollMode}"
                                      HorizontalScrollBarVisibility="{TemplateBinding ScrollViewer.HorizontalScrollBarVisibility}"
                                      VerticalScrollMode="{TemplateBinding ScrollViewer.VerticalScrollMode}"
                                      VerticalScrollBarVisibility="{TemplateBinding ScrollViewer.VerticalScrollBarVisibility}"
                                      IsHorizontalRailEnabled="{TemplateBinding ScrollViewer.IsHorizontalRailEnabled}"
                                      IsVerticalRailEnabled="{TemplateBinding ScrollViewer.IsVerticalRailEnabled}"
                                      IsDeferredScrollingEnabled="{TemplateBinding ScrollViewer.IsDeferredScrollingEnabled}"
                                      Margin="{TemplateBinding BorderThickness}" Padding="{TemplateBinding Padding}"
                                      Foreground="{TemplateBinding Foreground}"
                                      IsTabStop="False" AutomationProperties.AccessibilityView="Raw" ZoomMode="Disabled"/>

                        <TextBlock x:Name="PlaceholderTextContentPresenter" Grid.Row="1" Grid.Column="0" Grid.ColumnSpan="2"
                                   Foreground="{Binding PlaceholderForeground, RelativeSource={RelativeSource TemplatedParent}, TargetNullValue={ThemeResource FieldPlaceholderBrush}}"
                                   Margin="{TemplateBinding BorderThickness}" Padding="{TemplateBinding Padding}"
                                   Text="{TemplateBinding PlaceholderText}" TextAlignment="{TemplateBinding TextAlignment}"
                                   TextWrapping="{TemplateBinding TextWrapping}" IsHitTestVisible="False"/>

                        <Button x:Name="DeleteButton" Grid.Row="1" Grid.Column="1" RequestedTheme="Dark"
                                Style="{StaticResource FieldClearButtonStyle}"
                                BorderThickness="{TemplateBinding BorderThickness}" CornerRadius="{TemplateBinding CornerRadius}"
                                Padding="{ThemeResource HelperButtonThemePadding}" IsTabStop="False" Visibility="Collapsed"
                                AutomationProperties.AccessibilityView="Raw" FontSize="{TemplateBinding FontSize}"
                                Width="30" VerticalAlignment="Stretch"/>

                        <!-- NumberBox's compact-mode indicator, shown by SpinButtonsPopup. -->
                        <TextBlock x:Name="PopupIndicator" Grid.Row="1" Grid.Column="2" RequestedTheme="Dark" Visibility="Collapsed"
                                   Margin="{StaticResource NumberBoxPopupIndicatorMargin}"
                                   Foreground="{ThemeResource NumberBoxPopupIndicatorForeground}"
                                   VerticalAlignment="Center" HorizontalAlignment="Center" FontSize="12" Text="&#xEC8F;"
                                   FontFamily="{ThemeResource SymbolThemeFontFamily}" AutomationProperties.AccessibilityView="Raw"/>

                        <ContentPresenter x:Name="DescriptionPresenter" Grid.Row="2" Grid.Column="0" Grid.ColumnSpan="3"
                                          Content="{TemplateBinding Description}"
                                          Foreground="{ThemeResource SystemControlDescriptionTextForegroundBrush}"
                                          AutomationProperties.AccessibilityView="Raw" x:Load="False"/>
                    </Grid>
                </ControlTemplate>
            </Setter.Value>
        </Setter>
    </Style>

    <!-- A text box that asks for nothing is a field, for the reason a bare button is a cap. -->
    <Style TargetType="TextBox" BasedOn="{StaticResource ConsoleFieldTextBoxStyle}"/>

    <!-- The password field: the same well, with WinUI's reveal button in place of the clear button. PasswordBox has
         no PlaceholderForeground, so the placeholder names the palette's grey itself. -->
    <Style TargetType="PasswordBox" BasedOn="{StaticResource DefaultPasswordBoxStyle}">
        <Setter Property="Foreground" Value="{ThemeResource FieldForegroundBrush}"/>
        <Setter Property="Background" Value="{ThemeResource FieldFaceBrush}"/>
        <Setter Property="BorderBrush" Value="{ThemeResource FieldEdgeBrush}"/>
        <Setter Property="BorderThickness" Value="1"/>
        <Setter Property="CornerRadius" Value="{StaticResource CapCornerRadius}"/>
        <Setter Property="Padding" Value="11,8"/>
        <Setter Property="FontFamily" Value="{StaticResource ConsoleBodyFontFamily}"/>
        <Setter Property="FontSize" Value="13"/>
        <Setter Property="UseSystemFocusVisuals" Value="False"/>
        <Setter Property="Template">
            <Setter.Value>
                <ControlTemplate TargetType="PasswordBox">
                    <Grid x:Name="Root">

                        <Grid.Resources>
                            <!-- WinUI's reveal button, as it draws it. -->
                            <Style x:Key="FieldRevealButtonStyle" TargetType="ToggleButton">
                                <Setter Property="Template">
                                    <Setter.Value>
                                        <ControlTemplate TargetType="ToggleButton">
                                            <Grid x:Name="ButtonLayoutGrid" Margin="{ThemeResource TextBoxInnerButtonMargin}"
                                                  BorderBrush="{ThemeResource TextControlButtonBorderBrush}"
                                                  BorderThickness="{TemplateBinding BorderThickness}"
                                                  Background="{ThemeResource TextControlButtonBackground}"
                                                  CornerRadius="{TemplateBinding CornerRadius}">
                                                <VisualStateManager.VisualStateGroups>
                                                    <VisualStateGroup x:Name="CommonStates">
                                                        <VisualState x:Name="Normal"/>
                                                        <VisualState x:Name="Indeterminate"/>
                                                        <VisualState x:Name="PointerOver">
                                                            <VisualState.Setters>
                                                                <Setter Target="ButtonLayoutGrid.Background" Value="{ThemeResource TextControlButtonBackgroundPointerOver}"/>
                                                                <Setter Target="ButtonLayoutGrid.BorderBrush" Value="{ThemeResource TextControlButtonBorderBrushPointerOver}"/>
                                                                <Setter Target="GlyphElement.Foreground" Value="{ThemeResource TextControlButtonForegroundPointerOver}"/>
                                                            </VisualState.Setters>
                                                        </VisualState>
                                                        <VisualState x:Name="Pressed">
                                                            <VisualState.Setters>
                                                                <Setter Target="ButtonLayoutGrid.Background" Value="{ThemeResource TextControlButtonBackgroundPressed}"/>
                                                                <Setter Target="ButtonLayoutGrid.BorderBrush" Value="{ThemeResource TextControlButtonBorderBrushPressed}"/>
                                                                <Setter Target="GlyphElement.Foreground" Value="{ThemeResource TextControlButtonForegroundPressed}"/>
                                                            </VisualState.Setters>
                                                        </VisualState>
                                                        <VisualState x:Name="CheckedPressed">
                                                            <VisualState.Setters>
                                                                <Setter Target="ButtonLayoutGrid.Background" Value="{ThemeResource TextControlButtonBackgroundPressed}"/>
                                                                <Setter Target="ButtonLayoutGrid.BorderBrush" Value="{ThemeResource TextControlButtonBorderBrushPressed}"/>
                                                                <Setter Target="GlyphElement.Foreground" Value="{ThemeResource TextControlButtonForegroundPressed}"/>
                                                            </VisualState.Setters>
                                                        </VisualState>
                                                        <VisualState x:Name="IndeterminatePressed">
                                                            <VisualState.Setters>
                                                                <Setter Target="ButtonLayoutGrid.Background" Value="{ThemeResource TextControlButtonBackgroundPressed}"/>
                                                                <Setter Target="ButtonLayoutGrid.BorderBrush" Value="{ThemeResource TextControlButtonBorderBrushPressed}"/>
                                                                <Setter Target="GlyphElement.Foreground" Value="{ThemeResource TextControlButtonForegroundPressed}"/>
                                                            </VisualState.Setters>
                                                        </VisualState>
                                                        <!-- No Disabled state: WinUI's hid the reveal button on a locked field, but the field only
                                                             shows it while it is focused, and a locked field cannot be. So it is never seen locked,
                                                             and the field's own locked state dims everything in it. -->
                                                    </VisualStateGroup>
                                                </VisualStateManager.VisualStateGroups>
                                                <TextBlock x:Name="GlyphElement" Foreground="{ThemeResource TextControlButtonForeground}"
                                                           VerticalAlignment="Center" HorizontalAlignment="Center" FontStyle="Normal"
                                                           FontSize="{ThemeResource PasswordBoxIconFontSize}" Text="&#xF78D;"
                                                           FontFamily="{ThemeResource SymbolThemeFontFamily}"
                                                           AutomationProperties.AccessibilityView="Raw"/>
                                            </Grid>
                                        </ControlTemplate>
                                    </Setter.Value>
                                </Setter>
                            </Style>
                        </Grid.Resources>

                        <VisualStateManager.VisualStateGroups>
                            <VisualStateGroup x:Name="CommonStates">
                                <VisualState x:Name="Normal"/>
                                <VisualState x:Name="PointerOver"/>

                                <VisualState x:Name="Focused">
                                    <VisualState.Setters>
                                        <Setter Target="BorderElement.BorderBrush" Value="{ThemeResource ArmedEdgeBrush}"/>
                                        <Setter Target="FocusOutline.Opacity" Value="1"/>
                                    </VisualState.Setters>
                                </VisualState>

                                <VisualState x:Name="Disabled">
                                    <VisualState.Setters>
                                        <Setter Target="Root.Opacity" Value="{ThemeResource ConsoleDisabledOpacity}"/>
                                        <Setter Target="HeaderContentPresenter.Foreground" Value="{ThemeResource ConsoleDisabledForegroundBrush}"/>
                                        <Setter Target="ContentElement.Foreground" Value="{ThemeResource ConsoleDisabledFieldForegroundBrush}"/>
                                    </VisualState.Setters>
                                </VisualState>
                            </VisualStateGroup>

                            <VisualStateGroup x:Name="ButtonStates">
                                <VisualState x:Name="ButtonVisible">
                                    <VisualState.Setters>
                                        <Setter Target="RevealButton.Visibility" Value="Visible"/>
                                    </VisualState.Setters>
                                </VisualState>
                                <VisualState x:Name="ButtonCollapsed"/>
                            </VisualStateGroup>
                        </VisualStateManager.VisualStateGroups>

                        <Grid.RowDefinitions>
                            <RowDefinition Height="Auto"/>
                            <RowDefinition Height="*"/>
                            <RowDefinition Height="Auto"/>
                        </Grid.RowDefinitions>

                        <Grid.ColumnDefinitions>
                            <ColumnDefinition Width="*"/>
                            <ColumnDefinition Width="Auto"/>
                        </Grid.ColumnDefinitions>

                        <ContentPresenter x:Name="HeaderContentPresenter" Grid.Row="0" Grid.Column="0" Grid.ColumnSpan="2"
                                          Content="{TemplateBinding Header}" ContentTemplate="{TemplateBinding HeaderTemplate}"
                                          FontFamily="{StaticResource ConsoleTelemetryFontFamily}" FontSize="10"
                                          CharacterSpacing="120" FontWeight="Normal"
                                          Foreground="{ThemeResource SilverMuteBrush}" Margin="0,0,0,5"
                                          TextWrapping="Wrap" VerticalAlignment="Top"
                                          Visibility="Collapsed" x:DeferLoadStrategy="Lazy"/>

                        <Border x:Name="FocusOutline" Grid.Row="1" Grid.Column="0" Grid.ColumnSpan="2" Margin="-3"
                                BorderBrush="{ThemeResource ArmedDisplayBrush}" BorderThickness="2" CornerRadius="7"
                                Opacity="0" IsHitTestVisible="False"/>

                        <Border x:Name="BorderElement" Grid.Row="1" Grid.Column="0" Grid.RowSpan="1" Grid.ColumnSpan="2"
                                Background="{TemplateBinding Background}" BorderBrush="{TemplateBinding BorderBrush}"
                                BorderThickness="{TemplateBinding BorderThickness}" CornerRadius="{TemplateBinding CornerRadius}"
                                MinWidth="{ThemeResource TextControlThemeMinWidth}" MinHeight="{ThemeResource TextControlThemeMinHeight}"/>

                        <Border x:Name="Shade" Grid.Row="1" Grid.Column="0" Grid.ColumnSpan="2" Height="4" Margin="1,1,1,0"
                                VerticalAlignment="Top" CornerRadius="3,3,0,0"
                                Background="{ThemeResource FieldShadeTopBrush}" IsHitTestVisible="False"/>
                        <Border x:Name="Lip" Grid.Row="1" Grid.Column="0" Grid.ColumnSpan="2" Height="1" Margin="1,0,1,1"
                                VerticalAlignment="Bottom"
                                Background="{ThemeResource FieldLipBrush}" IsHitTestVisible="False"/>

                        <ScrollViewer x:Name="ContentElement" Grid.Row="1" Grid.Column="0" RequestedTheme="Dark"
                                      HorizontalScrollMode="{TemplateBinding ScrollViewer.HorizontalScrollMode}"
                                      HorizontalScrollBarVisibility="{TemplateBinding ScrollViewer.HorizontalScrollBarVisibility}"
                                      VerticalScrollMode="{TemplateBinding ScrollViewer.VerticalScrollMode}"
                                      VerticalScrollBarVisibility="{TemplateBinding ScrollViewer.VerticalScrollBarVisibility}"
                                      IsHorizontalRailEnabled="{TemplateBinding ScrollViewer.IsHorizontalRailEnabled}"
                                      IsVerticalRailEnabled="{TemplateBinding ScrollViewer.IsVerticalRailEnabled}"
                                      Margin="{TemplateBinding BorderThickness}" Padding="{TemplateBinding Padding}"
                                      IsTabStop="False" ZoomMode="Disabled" AutomationProperties.AccessibilityView="Raw"/>

                        <TextBlock x:Name="PlaceholderTextContentPresenter" Grid.Row="1" Grid.Column="0" Grid.ColumnSpan="2"
                                   Foreground="{ThemeResource FieldPlaceholderBrush}"
                                   Margin="{TemplateBinding BorderThickness}" Padding="{TemplateBinding Padding}"
                                   Text="{TemplateBinding PlaceholderText}" IsHitTestVisible="False"/>

                        <ToggleButton x:Name="RevealButton" Grid.Row="1" Grid.Column="1" RequestedTheme="Dark"
                                      Style="{StaticResource FieldRevealButtonStyle}"
                                      BorderThickness="{TemplateBinding BorderThickness}" CornerRadius="{TemplateBinding CornerRadius}"
                                      Padding="{ThemeResource HelperButtonThemePadding}" IsTabStop="False" Visibility="Collapsed"
                                      FontSize="{TemplateBinding FontSize}" VerticalAlignment="Stretch" Width="30"/>

                        <ContentPresenter x:Name="DescriptionPresenter" Grid.Row="2" Grid.Column="0" Grid.ColumnSpan="2"
                                          Content="{TemplateBinding Description}"
                                          Foreground="{ThemeResource SystemControlDescriptionTextForegroundBrush}"
                                          AutomationProperties.AccessibilityView="Raw" x:Load="False"/>
                    </Grid>
                </ControlTemplate>
            </Setter.Value>
        </Setter>
    </Style>

    <!-- The number field. NumberBox draws no well of its own: its InputBox is a TextBox, which WinUI points at a
         style of its own, so the field reaches it only through this template, which points InputBox at
         ConsoleFieldTextBoxStyle instead. NumberBox hands InputBox its edge, padding, radius, face and words by
         template binding, so they are set here, on the NumberBox, to the field's values.

         The rest is WinUI's template. Two things are left out of it: the theme dictionaries that re-point the spin
         buttons at the text box's button colours, because a theme dictionary belongs in a dictionary App.xaml
         merges itself (ConsoleDictionaryTests), and the popup state's redundant re-setting of InputBox's style.
         So the inline spinners are WinUI's repeat buttons in the dark theme, small keys on the dark well, and the
         compact popup's are WinUI's own on the popup's ground. Making them console caps is the spinners' own
         piece of work, not a field's.

         Locked, InputBox dims itself as every field does, so this dims what InputBox does not cover - the label
         and the inline spinners - rather than its whole root, which would dim the field twice. -->
    <Style TargetType="NumberBox">
        <Setter Property="Foreground" Value="{ThemeResource FieldForegroundBrush}"/>
        <Setter Property="BorderBrush" Value="{ThemeResource FieldEdgeBrush}"/>
        <Setter Property="BorderThickness" Value="1"/>
        <Setter Property="CornerRadius" Value="{StaticResource CapCornerRadius}"/>
        <Setter Property="Padding" Value="11,8"/>
        <Setter Property="FontFamily" Value="{StaticResource ConsoleBodyFontFamily}"/>
        <Setter Property="FontSize" Value="13"/>
        <Setter Property="Template">
            <Setter.Value>
                <ControlTemplate TargetType="NumberBox">
                    <Grid Height="{TemplateBinding Height}">

                        <!-- WinUI's own spin button styles are declared by x:Name, which nothing outside its
                             dictionary can find - asked for from here they throw as the number box lays out. So
                             they are restated, as WinUI writes them, where the buttons can reach them. -->
                        <Grid.Resources>
                            <Style x:Key="FieldSpinButtonStyle" TargetType="RepeatButton" BasedOn="{StaticResource DefaultRepeatButtonStyle}">
                                <Setter Property="IsTabStop" Value="False"/>
                                <Setter Property="MinWidth" Value="32"/>
                                <Setter Property="Padding" Value="0"/>
                                <Setter Property="VerticalAlignment" Value="Stretch"/>
                                <Setter Property="BorderThickness" Value="{ThemeResource NumberBoxSpinButtonBorderThickness}"/>
                                <Setter Property="FontSize" Value="12"/>
                                <Setter Property="FontFamily" Value="{ThemeResource SymbolThemeFontFamily}"/>
                            </Style>
                        </Grid.Resources>

                        <VisualStateManager.VisualStateGroups>
                            <VisualStateGroup x:Name="CommonStates">
                                <VisualState x:Name="Normal"/>

                                <VisualState x:Name="Disabled">
                                    <VisualState.Setters>
                                        <Setter Target="HeaderContentPresenter.Opacity" Value="{ThemeResource ConsoleDisabledOpacity}"/>
                                        <Setter Target="HeaderContentPresenter.Foreground" Value="{ThemeResource ConsoleDisabledForegroundBrush}"/>
                                        <Setter Target="UpSpinButton.Opacity" Value="{ThemeResource ConsoleDisabledOpacity}"/>
                                        <Setter Target="DownSpinButton.Opacity" Value="{ThemeResource ConsoleDisabledOpacity}"/>
                                    </VisualState.Setters>
                                </VisualState>
                            </VisualStateGroup>

                            <VisualStateGroup x:Name="SpinButtonStates">
                                <VisualState x:Name="SpinButtonsCollapsed"/>
                                <VisualState x:Name="SpinButtonsVisible">
                                    <VisualState.Setters>
                                        <Setter Target="DownSpinButton.Visibility" Value="Visible"/>
                                        <Setter Target="UpSpinButton.Visibility" Value="Visible"/>
                                        <Setter Target="InputEater.Visibility" Value="Visible"/>
                                        <Setter Target="InputBox.MinWidth" Value="{ThemeResource NumberBoxMinWidth}"/>
                                    </VisualState.Setters>
                                </VisualState>
                                <VisualState x:Name="SpinButtonsPopup"/>
                            </VisualStateGroup>

                            <VisualStateGroup x:Name="UpSpinButtonEnabledStates">
                                <VisualState x:Name="UpSpinButtonEnabled"/>
                                <VisualState x:Name="UpSpinButtonDisabled">
                                    <VisualState.Setters>
                                        <Setter Target="UpSpinButton.IsEnabled" Value="False"/>
                                        <Setter Target="PopupUpSpinButton.IsEnabled" Value="False"/>
                                    </VisualState.Setters>
                                </VisualState>
                            </VisualStateGroup>

                            <VisualStateGroup x:Name="DownSpinButtonEnabledStates">
                                <VisualState x:Name="DownSpinButtonEnabled"/>
                                <VisualState x:Name="DownSpinButtonDisabled">
                                    <VisualState.Setters>
                                        <Setter Target="DownSpinButton.IsEnabled" Value="False"/>
                                        <Setter Target="PopupDownSpinButton.IsEnabled" Value="False"/>
                                    </VisualState.Setters>
                                </VisualState>
                            </VisualStateGroup>
                        </VisualStateManager.VisualStateGroups>

                        <Grid.RowDefinitions>
                            <RowDefinition Height="Auto"/>
                            <RowDefinition Height="*"/>
                            <RowDefinition Height="Auto"/>
                        </Grid.RowDefinitions>

                        <Grid.ColumnDefinitions>
                            <ColumnDefinition Width="*"/>
                            <ColumnDefinition Width="Auto"/>
                            <ColumnDefinition Width="Auto"/>
                        </Grid.ColumnDefinitions>

                        <!-- The field label (:2312), as the text box draws it. -->
                        <ContentPresenter x:Name="HeaderContentPresenter" Grid.ColumnSpan="3"
                                          Content="{TemplateBinding Header}" ContentTemplate="{TemplateBinding HeaderTemplate}"
                                          FontFamily="{StaticResource ConsoleTelemetryFontFamily}" FontSize="10"
                                          CharacterSpacing="120" FontWeight="Normal"
                                          Foreground="{ThemeResource SilverMuteBrush}" Margin="0,0,0,5"
                                          TextWrapping="Wrap" VerticalAlignment="Top"
                                          Visibility="Collapsed" x:DeferLoadStrategy="Lazy"/>

                        <TextBox x:Name="InputBox" Grid.Row="1" Grid.ColumnSpan="3"
                                 Style="{StaticResource ConsoleFieldTextBoxStyle}"
                                 InputScope="{TemplateBinding InputScope}" PlaceholderText="{TemplateBinding PlaceholderText}"
                                 SelectionFlyout="{TemplateBinding SelectionFlyout}"
                                 SelectionHighlightColor="{TemplateBinding SelectionHighlightColor}"
                                 TextReadingOrder="{TemplateBinding TextReadingOrder}"
                                 PreventKeyboardDisplayOnProgrammaticFocus="{TemplateBinding PreventKeyboardDisplayOnProgrammaticFocus}"
                                 FontSize="{TemplateBinding FontSize}" FontWeight="{TemplateBinding FontWeight}"
                                 FontFamily="{TemplateBinding FontFamily}"
                                 BorderThickness="{TemplateBinding BorderThickness}" BorderBrush="{TemplateBinding BorderBrush}"
                                 Padding="{TemplateBinding Padding}" Foreground="{TemplateBinding Foreground}"
                                 TextAlignment="{TemplateBinding TextAlignment}" CornerRadius="{TemplateBinding CornerRadius}"/>

                        <Popup x:Name="UpDownPopup" Grid.Row="1" Grid.Column="1"
                               VerticalOffset="{ThemeResource NumberBoxPopupVerticalOffset}"
                               HorizontalOffset="{ThemeResource NumberBoxPopupHorizonalOffset}"
                               ShouldConstrainToRootBounds="False" HorizontalAlignment="Left">
                            <Grid x:Name="PopupContentRoot" Padding="6" Background="{ThemeResource NumberBoxPopupBackground}"
                                  BorderBrush="{ThemeResource NumberBoxPopupBorderBrush}"
                                  BorderThickness="{ThemeResource NumberBoxPopupBorderThickness}"
                                  CornerRadius="{ThemeResource OverlayCornerRadius}">
                                <Grid.Resources>
                                    <Style x:Key="FieldPopupSpinButtonStyle" TargetType="RepeatButton">
                                        <Setter Property="AutomationProperties.AccessibilityView" Value="Raw"/>
                                        <Setter Property="IsTabStop" Value="False"/>
                                        <Setter Property="Width" Value="36"/>
                                        <Setter Property="Height" Value="36"/>
                                        <Setter Property="Padding" Value="0"/>
                                        <Setter Property="BorderThickness" Value="{ThemeResource NumberBoxPopupSpinButtonBorderThickness}"/>
                                        <Setter Property="FontSize" Value="16"/>
                                        <Setter Property="FontFamily" Value="{ThemeResource SymbolThemeFontFamily}"/>
                                        <Setter Property="CornerRadius" Value="{ThemeResource ControlCornerRadius}"/>
                                    </Style>
                                </Grid.Resources>
                                <Grid.RowDefinitions>
                                    <RowDefinition Height="*"/>
                                    <RowDefinition Height="*"/>
                                </Grid.RowDefinitions>
                                <RepeatButton x:Name="PopupUpSpinButton" Style="{StaticResource FieldPopupSpinButtonStyle}"
                                              Margin="0,0,0,4" Content="&#xE70E;"/>
                                <RepeatButton x:Name="PopupDownSpinButton" Style="{StaticResource FieldPopupSpinButtonStyle}"
                                              Grid.Row="1" Content="&#xE70D;"/>
                            </Grid>
                        </Popup>

                        <Button x:Name="InputEater" Grid.Row="1" Grid.Column="1" Grid.ColumnSpan="2" Visibility="Collapsed"
                                HorizontalAlignment="Stretch" VerticalAlignment="Stretch" Margin="4,0,0,0" IsTabStop="False"
                                AutomationProperties.AccessibilityView="Raw">
                            <Button.Template>
                                <ControlTemplate TargetType="Button">
                                    <Grid Background="Transparent"/>
                                </ControlTemplate>
                            </Button.Template>
                        </Button>

                        <RepeatButton x:Name="UpSpinButton" Grid.Row="1" Grid.Column="1" RequestedTheme="Dark" Visibility="Collapsed"
                                      FontSize="{TemplateBinding FontSize}" Content="&#xE70E;"
                                      Style="{StaticResource FieldSpinButtonStyle}" Margin="4"
                                      CornerRadius="{TemplateBinding CornerRadius}"/>
                        <RepeatButton x:Name="DownSpinButton" Grid.Row="1" Grid.Column="2" RequestedTheme="Dark" Visibility="Collapsed"
                                      FontSize="{TemplateBinding FontSize}" Content="&#xE70D;"
                                      Style="{StaticResource FieldSpinButtonStyle}" Margin="0,4,4,4"
                                      CornerRadius="{TemplateBinding CornerRadius}"/>

                        <ContentPresenter x:Name="DescriptionPresenter" Grid.Row="2" Grid.ColumnSpan="3"
                                          Content="{TemplateBinding Description}"
                                          Foreground="{ThemeResource SystemControlDescriptionTextForegroundBrush}"
                                          AutomationProperties.AccessibilityView="Raw"/>
                    </Grid>
                </ControlTemplate>
            </Setter.Value>
        </Setter>
    </Style>
</ResourceDictionary>
